<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Two miners die in Western Deep rock fall.</title>
<headline>Two miners die in Western Deep rock fall.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two miners were killed and one remains missing after an underground rock fall at Western Deep Levels gold mine, the mine said on Friday.</p>
<p>The accident ocurred late Thursday night and the fall, which occurred in a gully at a depth of 3.2 kilometres, was triggered by an earth tremor measuring 2.8 in magnitude.</p>
<p>Two other miners were critically injured.</p>
<p>&quot;Rescue teams are continuing the search for the missing man. Further details will be released as they become available,&quot; the mine said.</p>
<p>A company spokeswoman said the rest of the mine was still working and it was too early to say how production had been affected by the accident.</p>
<p>&quot;At the moment we are concentrating on searching for the missing man,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>Western Deeps is the world's deepest gold mine and part of the Anglo American Corp of South Africa Ltd stable.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
